:{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/isEqualTo(message:)","title":"isEqualTo(message:)","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/isequalto(message:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isEqualTo"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"message"},{"kind":"text","text":": any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SwiftProtobuf7MessageP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Message"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","title":"Yorkie_V1_Tree